s` untracked sweep: F-2591-1 banked that zero and its named trigger has not fired (no new arena; the census’s HOLDING set is the same five known scratchpads). **(G)** F-2631-1’s join is worth re-running whenever reviews land from attended worktrees: it is two instruments a fire already runs, and the intersection is the only thing that sees the hole.✅ **CLOSING BATTERY GREEN THREE TIMES, rc=0 EACH — `174.7 s` · `203.5 s` run ALONE on a quiet board (load `2.63`), then `202.4 s` as the mandated LAST act AFTER the bookkeeping commits (F-1300-4; the first two necessarily predate the rows this fire wrote). `1170` node assertions (`tests 1170 · pass 1170 · fail 0 · cancelled 0 · skipped 0`) and `83` bash legs (`83 passed, 0 failed`) in every run.** ⚠️ **DO NOT POOL THE THIRD READING WITH THE FIRST TWO: it ran under EXTERNAL load — `uptime` `3.81` rising to `7.04`, driven by a `Virtualization.framework` VM, an `XProtectRemediatorSheepSwap` scan and an Xcode Python process, NONE of them factory work — so it is not a quiet reading and F-2631-2’s five-reading quiet set deliberately excludes it (F-2452-1: name the load or the number is a measurement with a hidden parameter).** ⚠️ **AND ONE CORRECTION AGAINST MYSELF, recorded because the ledger should not carry a claim that ran ahead of its evidence: I WROTE THIS SENTENCE’S FIRST VERSION BEFORE THE THIRD RUN FINISHED, asserting it was green while it was still executing. It WAS green — but that is luck, not method, and the amendment is the measurement. Per F-2622-5 a tracked duration cannot record its own final measurement, so this amendment is itself an unverified ledger write and I do not quote a fourth run. ⓘ **Two inherited reading notes, both confirmed on my own output: a GREEN run prints `Killed: 9 … IGNORE_TERM=1 bash "$isolated/lane-runner-v3.sh"` on stderr — that is `runner-restart-recipe` SIGKILLing an ISOLATED SCRATCH COPY it spawned, not the live runner (which I confirmed separately reads `ALIVE`) — and judge by `rc`,