# Eight Winds E2 repair run lands two rows and parks two after measured retries

This run supersedes the earlier uncertainty around the E2 row-repair outcome.

- Confirmed Steam Wrecker's single teal-lit gauge panel as body-left from both cardinal views.
- Added that body-side datum and rebuilt only the two Steam Wrecker diagonal prompts.
- Landed Steam Wrecker `nw` row 2 and Rail Tough `se` row 1.
- Parked Coal Thief `sw` row 0 and Steam Wrecker `se` row 1 after three changed-premise native-image attempts each; every otherwise viable take put the distinguishing prop on the wrong screen side, while one Steam take duplicated the panel.
- Preserved all eight required non-target rows byte-for-byte; ten of twelve total rows remain byte-identical because the two parked target rows were left untouched.
- Final windtable QA passed scale, seam, background, and duplicate checks. TypeScript and production build gates passed.

