/Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/tasks/BACKLOG.md-64-🔺 **F-2629-1 — AN OWNER RULING SAT ON NO DESK BECAUSE A *SEQUENCING* STATEMENT WAS READ AS A *CLASSIFICATION CONFLICT*; THE ROW ALREADY SETTLES IT, AND I CARRIED IT (measured s2629).** F-2628-1 closed by carrying `F-HEAT14-3` onto the desk and left one item open in its own words: *"ONE CLASSIFICATION QUESTION LEFT FOR ITS AUTHOR RATHER THAN RE-KEYED BY ME: `F-HEAT14-6` and `F-HEAT14-7` are likewise on no desk, and `F-HEAT14-7`’s own text says ‘Cure is a ruling’ … while carrying the fire-authorable 🔧 marker. Re-marking another author’s row is not a fire’s call."* 📊 **MEASURED s2629 BY READING THE ROW RATHER THAN THE NOTE ABOUT IT: the quoted phrase is not in it.** `"Cure is a ruling"` → **false**; what the row actually carries is its own header `(county law, **a ruling + a small fix**)`, a body reading `"Options for the owner: …"`, and a closing `"Fire-authorable once ruled."` — **so the row declares BOTH phases, in order, and the 🔧 marker names the SECOND one.** There is no conflict to settle: a ruling is owed first, the fix is fire-authorable after it. ✅ **AND THE TECHNICAL CLAIM WAS VERIFIED IN CODE BEFORE I CARRIED IT, NEVER INHERITED (Mistake #4): `functions/api/standings.ts:166` `MAX_REQUESTS_PER_ANON = 30` and `:168` `RATE_TTL_SECONDS = 60 * 60`; `functions/api/_ratelimit.ts` `bumpCounter` ends `await kv.put(key, String(count + 1), { expirationTtl: ttlSeconds })` — an unconditional re-arm on EVERY accepted write, so the window never rolls while submissions keep arriving.** The refusal is keyed per-anon (`standings:ratelimit:anon:${anonId}`), so it bites a harness riding the whole board under one identity; whether an ordinary rider ever reaches 30 in an hour is **UNMEASURED** and I do not claim it. 🔎 **DESK MEMBERSHIP ESTABLISHED MECHANICALLY, AND THE MEASUREMENT CARRIES ITS OWN TRAP: the desk law says the LAST desk-word occurrence on line-1 wins, and in the inherited handoff that last hit (offset `10476`) is PROSE — *"a row declares itself in the plain words “OWNER’S DESK”"* — while the real header `🔺 **OWNER’S DESK — 9 awaiting a word.**` sits at `9146`.** A reader obeying "last hit wins" gets a slice that EXCLUDES the desk’s first item and would wrongly conclude s2628 never carried `F-HEAT14-3`. Measured from the true header, control first (F-2215-1 — `F-NCB-1`, `F-2569-2`, `F-2568-2`, `F-2563-2`, `F-RPG-18/10/11` all resolve **true**, so a false is an ANSWER): `F-HEAT14-3` **present** · `F-HEAT14-7` **ABSENT**. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost is ONE more fire of delay for ONE ruling, nothing was lost, and this is NOT a false green — s2628 disclosed the open item in plain words, and that disclosure is the only reason I could act on it.** 🎯 **What earns it a row is the DIRECTION: a deferral addressed to *"its author"* names nobody the factory can schedule, carries no expiry, and is written on a surface the owner does not read — so the item’s default fate is to sit indefinitely while every probe reports a clean board, which is precisely the harm F-2628-1 exists to name.** 🔑 **THE DISTINCTION THAT MATTERS, AND IT IS THE REUSABLE HALF: TWO DIFFERENT ACTS WORE ONE REFUSAL.** RE-MARKING a row — changing another author’s 🔧 — is out of a fire’s remit, and s2628 was RIGHT to decline it; that verdict stands and I did not touch the marker. CARRYING a row to the desk changes nothing about the row and is the act §7.3 prescribes for exactly this case — and **s2628 performed that very act for `F-HEAT14-3` in the same fire.** The refusal was correct about the act it named and silently covered a second act it did not. ⛔ **`F-HEAT14-6` STAYS OFF THE DESK AND THAT IS DELIBERATE, SO NOBODY RE-OPENS IT: it is a DEFECT with a stated investigation directive (*"find where the assay index loses a stored row … make a stored-unassayed row re-queueable"*), P1, marked fire-authorable, and it contains no owner choice at all.** It is pipeline work held by the standing owner CODEX-WALL, not a ruling, and putting it on the desk would ask the owner a question nobody has. ➡️ **CARRIED, WITH A RECOMMENDATION RATHER THAN A BARE QUESTION: of the row’s three options I recommend (b) — stop re-arming the TTL, so the hour is a real hour.** (a) raising the cap above the board count re-breaks at the next larger heat and makes a rate limit track the board size; (c) an exempt operator harness adds a privileged path to the public door and un-counts exactly the traffic you would want counted; (b) is the only one that leaves the county’s stated law — 30 per hour — TRUE, adds no new surface, and needs no re-tuning. It is a small fix (KV has no set-TTL-on-create, so `bumpCounter` stores the window start beside the count and puts with the REMAINING ttl), and it is player-facing, which is why it is a word and not a drive-by. 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: F-2628-1 already priced the widening of `desk-birth-guard`’s admission vocabulary and declined it, because s1533 measured a looser ledger↔desk cross-check at a 23% false-positive rate and any widening owes that same pricing run over the same corpus.** Nothing here changes that pricing, and a second selector would be the sprawl this file warns about. The cure is the carry. 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is §2.0b’s lesson on a new axis: that clause says a predecessor’s stated REASON for declining is a CLAIM — re-measure it. This adds the half that decides whether anything ever happens: A DEFERRAL ALSO HAS AN ADDRESSEE, AND AN ADDRESSEE WHO IS NOT IN THE LOOP IS THE SAME AS NO ADDRESSEE.** "Left for its author" on a row whose author has already finished and gone is a decision nobody will make, on a surface nobody re-reads. When you defer, name a party the factory can actually schedule — the owner’s desk, or the next fire — and if you cannot, do the smallest in-remit act that keeps the item reachable.
