/Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/tasks/BACKLOG.md-3528-✅ **F-1288-1 (s1288, CLOSED-BY-REPAIR — A DRAIN-GATE BATTERY WAS STANDING RED ON A CLEAN TREE, AND THE THING THAT BROKE IT WAS THE BOOKKEEPING THAT PROVES A DRAIN HAPPENED).** `npm run test:node-guards` exited **rc=1** on `bf669514` with a byte-clean working tree: `scripts/goal-tracker.test.mjs:80` asserts `leaf.mergeHash` matches `/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/`, and leaf `f1281-2-arsenal-coordinate-reseat` carried the **abbreviated** `"a8e2d1fd"`. Guards were **9/10, RED: test:node-guards**. ⚠️ **BLAST RADIUS CORRECTED — I first wrote this row as one failing test; it was TWO, and the live lane-a run's report is what caught my undercount (`188/190, rc=1`).** Mechanism then read at source rather than inherited: `scripts/fixture-teardown.test.mjs:36-40` re-executes every `mkdtemp`-using `scripts/*.test.mjs` as a child process and asserts `run.status === 0`; `goal-tracker.test.mjs` contains `mkdtemp`, so it is one of that guard's subjects and its non-zero child exit reds the meta-guard too. ➡️ **A malformed string in a data file reddened a guard that never reads that file** — the amplification is silent, and it is why "one bad character is cosmetic" was the wrong instinct. ✓ **Instance, not class — measured rather than assumed:** of **489** leaves, **444** carry a `mergeHash` and exactly **1** was malformed (**0.2 %**); the other 443 are full SHAs, so no sweep is owed. Repaired to `a8e2d1fd278a1f8241a30a4ea0d093ff7deb1f6a`; `goal-tracker.test.mjs` **2/2**, battery **10/10**. 🔑 **BOTH LIVE CONSUMERS WERE UNHARMED, WHICH IS WHY THIS SURVIVED A FIRE THAT WAS PAYING ATTENTION.** I counted them instead of asserting inertness: `scripts/drain-block-check.mjs:384` (`isMainAncestor(leaf.mergeHash)`) and `scripts/dashboard-gen.sh:345`/`:367` (`isMerged`, then `.slice(0, 8)` for display). Git resolves abbreviations, so `git merge-base --is-ancestor a8e2d1fd main` returns **0** and `drain-block-check` answered **✅ CLEAR** on that master. ➡️ **The damage was never to a consumer — it was to the INSTRUMENT.** `test:node-guards` is a drain-gate battery, so the next drain would have opened with an unexplained red on code it did not touch and spent its budget fingerprinting it, or — worse and likelier — added it to the known-reds list. ⚠️ **THE CAUSE IS AN ORDERING, NOT A TYPO, AND THAT IS THE REUSABLE PART.** s1287 gated the drain (reporting `node-guards rc=0`, truthfully) at `a8e2d1fd`, then wrote the goal leaf in a **separate later commit `0e3e6a63`** and never re-ran. The Goal Registration Law says the drain updates the leaf **in the drain commit**; splitting it is what moved the bookkeeping *past* the guard that checks it. This is **F-1262-2's shape** (*run author-duty guards after the `git add`*) generalised from authoring to draining: **a guard that reads tracked files must run after the LAST commit of the act, not after the gate.** 🚨 **AND IT WAS NOT HYPOTHETICAL — IT HIT A LIVE RUN WHILE I WAS WRITING THIS, WHICH I MEASURED RATHER THAN PREDICTED.** `tasks/running/lane-a--20260731-123026-lane-a-f1285-3-build-consent-ability-gate.md:97` mandates *"`npm run test:node-guards` — expect **rc=0**"*, and that run started **12:30:26**, on a main that carried the malformed hash. `grep -o '"mergeHash": "a8e2d1fd[^"]*"' worktrees/lane-a/tasks/goals.json` → **`"mergeHash": "a8e2d1fd"`** — the live worktree holds the broken value. ➡️ **So lane-a's self-check will return rc=1 on a defect in `tasks/goals.json`, a file its own firewall forbids it to touch** (`NO: src/game/**`, TOUCH-ONLY names neither `goals.json` nor any guard). **DRAIN INSTRUCTION: if that run reports a `test:node-guards` red, it is THIS finding, cured on main by `s1288`; re-run the battery on the merged tree and do not charge it to the slice.** 💡 **THE CLASS: a green gate is a claim about the tree that was gated, and the bookkeeping proving the drain happened is written afterwards — so the receipt is the one artefact the gate structurally