DED-OWNED trees (🧮 DERIVE IT WITH `node scripts/modified-tracked-evidence-census.mjs`; the predicate is the **AT RISK** bucket, NOT the wider non-SAFE union which reads `1530` / `1798.8 MB` / `27` trees — F-2585-1). **RE-MEASURED s2625: `482` / `447.9 MB` / `25` trees, still ZERO factory-side** (the chain is 421 → 431 → 492 → 516 → 480 → 480 → 492 → 480 → 487 → 480 → **482**, ordinary attended churn, NOT a new exposure and NOT a partial discharge). **The case for LEAVING them is stated first and is strong:** every path is TRACKED so a committed version already exists, ~49% is churn-like, and the RETENTION LAW's own owner amendment of 2026-08-26 (*"keep the run logs local for now"*) already exempted a 2.4 GB evidence class from the mirror-into-git half. **RECOMMENDATION: salvage only the DIMENSION-CHANGE and ≥2%-delta classes (~198 files, ~250 MB est.) to a parentless `save/*` ref; let the churn go.** A fire will execute that on one word and will not do it unasked. 🔺 **F-2568-2** — abolish the hand-moved `CURRENT_ROTATION_ID`, or keep the weekly edit? The answer is already derivable from shipped data (`functions/api/standings.ts:1188` `currentOrLatestRotation` filters `opensAt <= now`); only the landing page re-states it by hand, once a week, forever. 🔺 **F-2563-2** — `19.86 GB` across `13` local-only refs, ~92% on attended-owned refs (`sol/*`, `drain/sprites-roster`); push, or leave local? No fire pushes these unilaterally. **RE-MEASURED s2625 by F-2563-1's own method (tip membership in `rev-list --remotes`, never a name match; controls `553` local heads / `13,840` remote-reachable commits): `16` refs, of which `refs/heads/main` was only my own unpushed lock commit — so `15` excluding it, against the banked `13` — and the union unique to them is `30,436` blobs / `19.48 GB`.** ⚠️ **Read the DIRECTION before the number: the REF COUNT ROSE while the BYTES FELL, so this is NOT growth and must not be reported as such; and per F-2563-1 do NOT sum the per-ref figures, which double-count. The new members include today's live `heat14/era6-reride` (F-2625-1).** 🔺 **F-RPG-18** A14 the Regatta's racing body (a spec slice first) · 🔺 **F-RPG-10** A15 the Long Road's convoy stop (default stands until he plays it) · 🔺 **F-RPG-11** A16 Moth Season's choice (default stands until he plays it). 🔺 **F-HEAT14-7** — **the county’s hour never rolls, so a rider can be locked out of the board for good (carried s2629; born in the attended heat-14 drain, on no desk until now — F-2629-1).** `functions/api/standings.ts:166` caps an anon at `30` submissions per `RATE_TTL_SECONDS = 3600`, and `functions/api/_ratelimit.ts` `bumpCounter` re-arms that hour on EVERY accepted write — verified by reading both files, not inherited — so under sustained traffic the window never expires: ride 37’s own reel (`e10-archive-world`, a first-ever secure) was refused `rate_limited`. The row offers three options and I recommend **(b) stop re-arming the TTL, so the hour is a real hour**: (a) raising the cap above the board count re-breaks at the next larger heat and makes a rate limit track the board size, (c) an exempt operator harness adds a privileged path to the public door and un-counts exactly the traffic you would want counted, and (b) is the only one that leaves the stated law — 30 per hour — TRUE with no new surface and no re-tuning. It is a small fix (`bumpCounter` stores the window start beside the count and puts with the REMAINING ttl), and it is fire-authorable the moment you rule; it is player-facing, which is why it is a word and not a drive-by. 🔺 **F-2632-2** — **should `fire-runner.sh:97` be repaired, and if so surgically? (new s2632, with F-2632-1.)** That line means to force a real fire when a lock line is STRANDED, so §1.1’s dead-lock takeover happens promptly — and measured, its literal `grep -q "lock<SP>ACTIVE"` misses **~96.5%** of real lock line-1s (18/500 and 33/1017 on two independent denominators) and has been dead since **2026-08-05**. **Leaving it 