r's desk was on no board Robin reads** — F-1333-3's Completeness breach, one fire's worth of it, generalised. F-1328-3 — *"says the word"*, a **one-word** owner decision — sat invisible for **six fires** while three consecutive handoffs listed it as awaiting that word. It is named on four lines of the ledger and was still invisible: **every one of those lines belongs to a different finding that cites it.** ➡️ **Backfilled with its owner question quoted verbatim from the s1328 handoff.** ✅ **(D) SHIPPED THE GUARD THE REFUTED ONE WAS REACHING FOR: `scripts/desk-declaration-guard.mjs`, 12 tests, rooted in `test:node-guards` + `test:ledger-guards`, `gate-caller-audit` PASS.** One question on one axis — *does the row exist?* — with today's **9** as a named grandfathered baseline (the F-1259-1 pattern), and **exit 2 rather than PASS** when it cannot find the desk or the desk holds no F-IDs. **Proven by manufacturing each violation, never by a green:** no-row → 1 · mention-inside-another-row (the F-1328-3 shape) → 1 · id past the 90-char zone → 1 · missing desk → 2 · empty desk → 2. **One test drives the same row through 🟡/🔺/🔴/✅ and demands all four PASS, so F-1334-1's refutation is now enforced in code rather than only written down.** 🪞 **(E) THE GUARD IMMEDIATELY CAUGHT ITS OWN AUTHOR — TWICE — AND BOTH TIMES MY PUBLISHED NUMBER WAS THE WRONG ONE.** ⑴ **Denominator:** my scratch probe anchored each id to a preceding marker glyph, so it saw only desk items introduced by their own 🔺/🟡/🔻 and reported a desk of **35**. The desk also routes ids in shared runs — *"F-1242-1 + F-1193-2"*, *"F-1327-1/F-1329-2"*, *"F-1253-1/2/3"*. Counting every F-ID gives **43**, and among the 8 I could not see was **one more undeclared item, F-1193-2** — riding inside F-1242-1's row, invisible for precisely the F-1328-3 reason. **I had already written "9 of 35 (26%)" into the ledger; the guard corrected it to 10 of 43 (23%) and I corrected the row.** ⑵ **Vacuous green:** the first draft's entrypoint test was ``import.meta.url === `file://${process.argv[1]}` `` — **false in this repo, because the path contains a space** that `import.meta.url` percent-encodes and `argv[1]` does not. The guard **ran as a no-op and exited 0**: a silent pass that read nothing, the exact failure mode `gate-caller-audit` exists to prevent, and it would have shipped green. Caught by running it before trusting it; now pinned by a test whose fixture directory has a space in its name. ⓘ **A third disagreement, earlier: my first "declaring row" test was *ID appears in the 90-char zone*, which credited F-1328-3 with two rows belonging to other findings — the identical conflation I was filing F-1333-2 for. Fixing it is what turned "marker mismatch" into "the row does not exist."** ✅ **(F) DUTIES, EACH CHECKED AT ITS OWN SOURCE.** **ASSAYER 0** (`pending/` empty). **TICKER 0 owed** — `ticker-digest-2026-07-31.md` exists and its header names 2026-07-31 as the coverage day. **GAZETTE 0, correctly** — nothing player-visible merged. **DEPLOY skipped LAWFULLY** — no gameplay code; guard + ledger only. **ART-SLOT audit not owed** — never touched the slot; s1332's numbers stand (**AT RISK 748 files / 566.47 MB**, still F-1331-4). **BACKUP pushed.** **LEDGER GUARD BATTERY as my last act** per F-1300-4: 50 node tests + all five guard scripts green, `double-state 0`, `desk-declaration 43/34/9 PASS`. 🏜️ **(G) PIPELINE-DRY: lane-a, lane-c, lane-d — unchanged, and I did NOT re-derive it (s1333 §I(1) is explicit and its retirements are committed at `db84f960`).** I authored no master: every candidate remains shipped, owner-gated, or blocked. ➡️ **(H) NEXT FIRE, IN ORDER. (1) The board is owner-blocked, not idle-by-accident — the single highest-value act is still nagging F-1330-1 (ONE WORD unblocks green branch `7c4f132f`, rec (a)); it also unjams F-1329-2's manifest slice and `e1-twin-banks` behind lane-b's five held files.** **(2) DO NOT build a marker-equality guard — F-1334-1 is a measured refutation, not an opinion; if you find yourself drafting it, you are re-deriving 24-of-35.** **(3) Cheap, real, fire-authorable: retire grandfathered entries from `desk-declaration-guard`'s list by giving those 9 findings rows.** Each is one row and the guard tells you the moment one is done. Start with **F-1193-2** and **F-1120-2** (the latter is cited on nine lines and still undeclared). **(4)** Do NOT author the per-run-output-dir cure (🔺 F-1328-3 — it now has a row, which is **visibility, not clearance**; its GATE line says OWNER) or any census corrective (🔺 F-1331-2). **(5)** Do NOT reset lane-b. **(6) If you edit STATUS's desk list, note the new coupling: the guard's test asserts every grandfathered id is still ON the desk, so carry the prior list forward verbatim.** **(7) This §H is a hypothesis like every §H before it.** 🔺 **OWNER DESK — the board is DRY ON ALL FOUR LANES and unblocking it is entirely owner-side; F-1330-1 is the cheapest word you can spend.** New: **F-1334-2 SHIPPED same fire, no ask.** F-1333-2's ask is **withdrawn — refuted, see F-1334-1.** Carried: 🔺 **F-1333-2 superseded** · 🔺 **F-1332-2** · 🟡 **F-1332-1**. All prior carry unchanged: 🔺 **F-1331-4 (566 MB unstored, rule on `motion-pilot`)** · 🔺 **F-1331-2** · 🔺 **F-1330-1 (one word, rec (a))** · 🔺 **F-1329-1** · 🔺 **F-1328-3** · 🔺 **F-1327-1/F-1329-2** · 🔺 **F-1315-2** · 🔺 **F-1313-3** (rec (b)) · 🔺 **F-1313-2** · 🔺 **F-1312-2** · 🔺 `rf-34` (rec **A**) · 🔺 `vp-02e-jumper` · 🔺 `e1-hold-the-claim` · 🔺 **F-1302-2** · 🔺 F-1300-3 · 🔺 **F-1279-2 rec L2** · 🔺 F-1295-1 · 🔺 **F-1101-1 RETIRE THE THREAD** · 🔺 F-1120-2 (1b) · 🔺 F-1287-1 + F-1286-2 · 🔺 plist `ProcessType` (F-1270-4) · 🔺 F-1267-3 · 🔺 F-1242-1 + F-1193-2 · 🔺 F-1260-3 · 🔺 **F-1252-1** · 🔺 F-1257-4 · 🔺 F-1255-4/1 · 🔺 F-1254-3 · 🔺 F-1253-1/2/3 · 🔺 **F-1162-1 / F-1242-2 — 168th ask** · 🔺 F-1193-3 · 🔺 gold-per-token · 🔺 F-1209-3 · 🔺 TOWN ZOOM clamps · 🔺 F-1185-1 · 🔺 F-1208-3 · 🔺 F-1204-1 · 🔺 **F-1141-3+F-1164-1** · 🔻 F-1182-2 `brew upgrade codex` (151st). 💡 **THE THROUGH-LINE, AND IT IS s1333'S OWN LESSON TURNED ON ITS AUTHOR: s1333 proved that a "NEXT" line is a claim with an expiry date and nothing expires it. Its own §I was a "NEXT" line. It expired in under an hour.** The recommendation was careful, specific, evidence-backed and **wrong** — not because s1333 was careless, but because a *cure* proposed from the outside carries no measurement of its own false-positive rate, and nothing in the handoff format asks for one. ➡️ **A finding is a measurement; the cure attached to it is a hypothesis wearing the finding's authority.** s1333 measured the disagreement honestly and then, in the same breath, proposed equating the two things it had just proved were different. **The fix is not more care — it is that the first act on any inherited cure is to measure the cure, not to build it.** Ten minutes of counting turned the board's top recommendation into a refutation and a better guard. 🪞 **And the same blade cut me three times in one fire** — narrow denominator, loose discriminator, no-op entrypoint — each caught only because an instrument disagreed with a number I had *already written down*. *The value of shipping a mechanism instead of a sweep is that it keeps disagreeing with you after the fire that built it has gone.*
