* If you must author, **F-1333-2's marker guard** is the one genuinely unowned, uncollided, non-owner-gated slice I found. **(4)** Do NOT author the per-run-output-dir cure (🔺 F-1328-3, owner's desk — see §E) or any census corrective (🔺 F-1331-2). **(5)** Do NOT reset lane-b. **(6)** This §I is a hypothesis like every §I before it. 🔺 **OWNER DESK — the board is now DRY ON ALL FOUR LANES and unblocking it is entirely owner-side; F-1330-1 is the cheapest word you can spend.** New: **F-1333-2** (add the marker guard?). Backfilled and now visible for the first time: 🔺 **F-1332-2** · 🟡 **F-1332-1**. All prior carry unchanged: 🔺 **F-1331-4 (566 MB unstored, rule on `motion-pilot`)** · 🔺 **F-1331-2** · 🔺 **F-1330-1 (one word, rec (a))** · 🔺 **F-1329-1** · 🔺 **F-1328-3** · 🔺 **F-1327-1/F-1329-2** · 🔺 **F-1315-2** · 🔺 **F-1313-3** (rec (b)) · 🔺 **F-1313-2** · 🔺 **F-1312-2** · 🔺 `rf-34` (rec **A**) · 🔺 `vp-02e-jumper` · 🔺 `e1-hold-the-claim` · 🔺 **F-1302-2** · 🔺 F-1300-3 · 🔺 **F-1279-2 rec L2** · 🔺 F-1295-1 · 🔺 **F-1101-1 RETIRE THE THREAD** · 🔺 F-1120-2 (1b) · 🔺 F-1287-1 + F-1286-2 · 🔺 plist `ProcessType` (F-1270-4) · 🔺 F-1267-3 · 🔺 F-1242-1 + F-1193-2 · 🔺 F-1260-3 · 🔺 **F-1252-1** · 🔺 F-1257-4 · 🔺 F-1255-4/1 · 🔺 F-1254-3 · 🔺 F-1253-1/2/3 · 🔺 **F-1162-1 / F-1242-2 — 167th ask** · 🔺 F-1193-3 · 🔺 gold-per-token · 🔺 F-1209-3 · 🔺 TOWN ZOOM clamps · 🔺 F-1185-1 · 🔺 F-1208-3 · 🔺 F-1204-1 · 🔺 **F-1141-3+F-1164-1** · 🔻 F-1182-2 `brew upgrade codex` (150th). 💡 **THE THROUGH-LINE: s1332 learned that a QA criterion is only as true as the frame it was measured in. Mine is one layer further out — A LEDGER LINE THAT NAMES THE *NEXT* THING IS A CLAIM WITH AN EXPIRY DATE, AND NOTHING IN THIS FACTORY EXPIRES IT.** ✅ lines retire when the work merges, because the merge is the event that writes them. **"NEXT" lines have no such event** — the merge that consumes a rung happens somewhere else, under a different name, and never comes back to cross it out. So `perf-05` sat advertised as lane-a's next rung for **294 fires after it shipped**, and F-1313-1 kept recommending `the-claim` first **after `the-claim` had merged and after its own premise had been overturned**. ➡️ *The factory has a law for retiring finished work and no law for retiring finished INSTRUCTIONS — and an instruction outlives its truth silently, because nothing about it looks stale.* 🪞 **And the mirror, which is the part I would rather not write: I nearly shipped the same defect this fire.** My instinct on three confident agent reports was to pick the best one and queue it — they were thorough, they cited files, they read like evidence. **They were reports about a ledger, not about main.** The only thing that separated a good refill from a 824k-token flail was four `merge-base --is-ancestor` probes costing about ten seconds. *An inherited claim does not become verified by being well-argued, and my own agents are exactly as inheritable as any dead fire's handoff.*
