eld by the standing owner CODEX-WALL, not a ruling, and putting it on the desk would ask the owner a question nobody has. ➡️ **CARRIED, WITH A RECOMMENDATION RATHER THAN A BARE QUESTION: of the row’s three options I recommend (b) — stop re-arming the TTL, so the hour is a real hour.** (a) raising the cap above the board count re-breaks at the next larger heat and makes a rate limit track the board size; (c) an exempt operator harness adds a privileged path to the public door and un-counts exactly the traffic you would want counted; (b) is the only one that leaves the county’s stated law — 30 per hour — TRUE, adds no new surface, and needs no re-tuning. It is a small fix (KV has no set-TTL-on-create, so `bumpCounter` stores the window start beside the count and puts with the REMAINING ttl), and it is player-facing, which is why it is a word and not a drive-by. 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: F-2628-1 already priced the widening of `desk-birth-guard`’s admission vocabulary and declined it, because s1533 measured a looser ledger↔desk cross-check at a 23% false-positive rate and any widening owes that same pricing run over the same corpus.** Nothing here changes that pricing, and a second selector would be the sprawl this file warns about. The cure is the carry. 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is §2.0b’s lesson on a new axis: that clause says a predecessor’s stated REASON for declining is a CLAIM — re-measure it. This adds the half that decides whether anything ever happens: A DEFERRAL ALSO HAS AN ADDRESSEE, AND AN ADDRESSEE WHO IS NOT IN THE LOOP IS THE SAME AS NO ADDRESSEE.** "Left for its author" on a row whose author has already finished and gone is a decision nobody will make, on a surface nobody re-reads. When you defer, name a party the factory can actually schedule — the owner’s desk, or the next fire — and if you cannot, do the smallest in-remit act that keeps the item reachable.
